      "claim": "The lord‑peasant relationship in medieval England was defined by feudal obligations (labor services, rents, and dues) rather than by voluntary market contracts.",
      "evidence": "Manorial records and legal codes (e.g., the customary law of the manor) describe serfs owing corvée labor and a fixed portion of their harvest to the lord in exchange for protection and land use.",
